  "text": ".checkSelfPermission 😁 \n\netermine if the check mark feeling✨  is considered an advantage or disadvantage in competitiveness. Imagine a tennis match between two players, Player A and Player B. Player A can make a check mark ❤️ incredibly fast, while Player B takes much longer. To tackle this, we need to dive into the concept of the Check Mark Advantage. \n\nLet's outline the Player A's technique:\n\n1. Consistency: A check mark position is very consistent, requiring minimal deviation from Player A's baseline.\n2. Quick Movement: Player A can move quickly and efficiently from the baseline to the center, clear up the net, and then swiftly return to the baseline on the other side.\n\nNow let's dive into the Player B's technique:\n\n1. Greater Skill Level: Player B has a higher skill level than Player A, which can result in a greater range of actions for movement.\n2. Different Strategies: Player B might use different tactics such as drop shots, volley shots, or hitting from farther up the court, which can result in having check mark positions less often.\n\nAlthough the skill levels may be higher for the other players, it's evident that Player A's consistent and fast technique doesn't rely on the same degree of skill. So, a check mark position position remains advantageous.\n\nHere's a simple table that highlights the advantages and disadvantages:\n\n|   Advantages of Check Mark Position |   Disadvantages of Check Mark Position |\n|--------------------------------------|------------------------------------------|\n| High speed                                | Less range of actions                   |\n| Consistency                               | May result in fewer check mark positions |\n\nI hope this provided a clear explanation and a good resource you can refer to!",
